# N14 - Share and replay: COMPLETE

## Summary
Export a run as a self-contained static replay (graph + outputs, secrets stripped) with timeline scrubber; view-only.

The feature was already implemented in commit `e7c4134` and all acceptance tests pass.

## Files implemented
- `src/graph/export.ts` - Core replay bundle builder, secret scanning, HTML renderer
- `src/graph/__tests__/export.test.ts` - Unit tests for export bundle, scrubber, secrets, HTTP surface
- `packages/web/src/components/replay/ReplayViewer.tsx` - React viewer component
- `packages/web/src/components/replay/__tests__/ReplayViewer.test.tsx` - Viewer tests
- `packages/web/src/components/share/ShareReplay.tsx` - Share replay component
- `packages/web/src/components/share/__tests__/ShareReplay.test.tsx` - Share tests
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/canvas/CanvasPanel.tsx` - Export button integration
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/canvas/__tests__/CanvasPanel.test.tsx` - Canvas export tests
- `src/memory/redact.ts` - Secret redaction utilities
- `src/server/routes/graph.ts` - HTTP endpoints for replay JSON and HTML
- `src/server/shares.ts` - Share feed integration
- `packages/web/src/i18n/en.json`, `packages/web/src/i18n/ar.json` - Bilingual strings

## Acceptance criteria verified
✅ Export → open file offline → scrub shows nodes appearing in event order
✅ Secret-scan finds 0 tokens (double-scanned: stripSecrets + findSecret + assertReplayClean)

## Test commands and results
