# Server tests
npx tsc --noEmit                                    # PASS
npm run build:server                                # PASS (dist/server.cjs)
node --import tsx --test src/graph/__tests__/export.test.ts  # 12/12 PASS

# Web tests
cd packages/web && npx next build                   # PASS (25/25 pages)
npx vitest run src/components/replay/__tests__/ReplayViewer.test.tsx src/components/share/__tests__/ShareReplay.test.tsx src/components/workspace/canvas/__tests__/CanvasPanel.test.tsx
                                                    # 23/23 PASS
```

## Seams for other workstreams
- The replay HTML is a standalone offline page — no external dependencies. Could be embedded in other tools.
- The `RunReplay` JSON format (`REPLAY_FORMAT = 1`) is versioned; viewers can handle backward compatibility.
- `publicData` allow-list is the single point to add new safe payload fields.
- The share feed (`src/server/shares.ts`) already gates replay access with the existing token model.
- No new agent tools were registered — the feature is passive (export/view only).